  "other_facts": "The study was performed at Jinling Hospital. It assessed whether glucose variability during acute pancreatitis predicts post-acute pancreatitis diabetes mellitus, which significantly affects patient quality of life. A Cox proportional hazards model was used to evaluate the association of glucose variability with developing PPDM-A. Restricted cubic splines characterized dose-response relationships of glucose variability with the 3-year probability of PPDM-A. Area under the receiver operating characteristic curves was used to assess predictive ability. The multivariate Cox association for LAGE had P <0.01. LAGE was measured during hospital stay. The authors concluded that LAGE accurately predicts PPDM-A and that further investigation is needed to determine whether glucose-variability-targeting interventions can confer favorable clinical outcomes.",
