  "other_facts": "The parent trial was the Telmisartan in the Management of Abdominal Aortic Aneurysm (TEDY) trial. Telmisartan is an angiotensin 1 receptor blocker. Of 207 participants recruited to TEDY, 124 were eligible for inclusion; 65 participants were included in the telmisartan group and 59 in the placebo group. Participants were randomised to receive telmisartan 40 mg or identical placebo. Computed tomography angiography was performed at entry and at least one other time point during the trial (12 or 24 months). Orthogonal abdominal aortic aneurysm diameter, peak wall stress, and peak wall rupture index were measured using previously validated methods. Annual change was compared using linear mixed effects models that were either unadjusted or adjusted for risk factors different at entry (p < .100) or systolic blood pressure at one year. The p value was .043 for peak wall stress and .032 for peak wall rupture index after adjustment for risk factors. After adjustment for systolic blood pressure at one year, telmisartan did not significantly reduce annual increases in peak wall stress or peak wall rupture index.",
