  "other_facts": "A rapid and sensitive direct infusion-nano-electrospray ionization mass spectrometry (DI-nESI-MS) method was developed for detection and quantification of ciprofloxacin and its metabolites in human saliva. Internal standard was tamoxifen. Samples were diluted with ionization solvent, centrifuged, and filtered. An aliquot of 4 μL of filtrate was loaded into a nanospray capillary. The nanospray capillary was fitted into an off-line ion source. The instrument acquired a two-minute run using a voltage of 1000 V in positive-ion detection mode. Quantification of ciprofloxacin used the ratio of ciprofloxacin peak intensity to internal standard peak intensity.",
