  "other_facts": "Mock DHP was performed for 120 min using hyperbilirubinic human plasma and blood obtained from plasmapheresis and exchange transfusion, respectively. Plasma and blood were separately circulated in a closed circuit simulating DHP using an adsorption column (Lixelle S-35) at a flow rate of 100 ml/min. TBIL and DBIL levels were measured at 10, 30, 60, and 120 min from arterial and venous ports and assessed with the Jendrassik-Grof method. All tests were performed in triplicate. The study was set up to test the bilirubin adsorption capacity of the Lixelle S-35 cartridge by DHP because limited options are available to treat critically ill patients with acute liver failure (ALF) and acute-on-chronic liver failure (AoCLF). The authors concluded that bilirubin adsorption rates after DHP were very promising for both hyperbilirubinic plasma and blood, that further in vitro investigations including comparisons with other techniques are required, and that the Lixelle S-35 should represent an option for the management of hyperbilirubinemia in ALF or AoCLF.",
