  "other_facts": "179 breast cancer units provided data. 13,741 of 188,909 patients (7.3%) met ACOSOG Z0011 inclusion criteria. The decrease in completion axillary lymph dissection from 2008 to 2015 was statistically significant (p < 0.001). In multivariable logistic regression analysis, factors associated with completion axillary lymph dissection were fewer removed sentinel lymph nodes, two tumour-affected sentinel lymph nodes, younger age, lower annual case volume per hospital, higher tumour grade, and lymphovascular invasion. No statistically significant influence was detected for hormone receptor or HER2 status. In the ACOSOG Z0011 trial, patients with 1 or 2 tumour-involved sentinel lymph nodes gained no benefit from completion axillary lymph dissection. Patients meeting ACOSOG Z0011 criteria could potentially have been spared the morbidity of completion axillary lymph dissection. Completion axillary lymph dissection tended to be performed in patients with higher axillary tumour burden. The study showed a shift towards less extensive axillary surgery through rapid implementation of clinical trial evidence into routine practice.",
