  "other_facts": "The prognostic relevance of direct contrast toxicity in TAVI patients remains unclear because of the confounding hemodynamic effect of acute left ventricular ejection fraction (LVEF) impairment on kidney function estimation. Different definitions of contrast-induced acute kidney injury (CI-AKI) may have different prognostic stratification potential. CI-AKI definition 1 was postprocedural creatinine increase of ≥0.3 mg/dl. CI-AKI definition 2 was postprocedural decrease of creatinine clearance of at least 25%. In Cox regression multivariate analysis, CI-AKI had p = 0.034 and LVEF had p = 0.012. LVEF and creatinine values at admission were not significantly associated with CI-AKI, but their interaction term significantly defined CI-AKI (p = 0.033). The prognostic accuracy of definition 2 was higher than definition 1 for the primary endpoint of 1-year mortality: area under the curve 0.704, p < 0.001; area under the curve 0.602, p = 0.037. The study concluded that in a nonselected patient population who underwent TAVI, CI-AKI was confirmed as an independent predictor of clinical outcome; only the interaction between LVEF and baseline creatinine values was found to determine CI-AKI; and the CI-AKI definition based on creatinine clearance values had higher prognostic accuracy than the CI-AKI definition based on creatinine absolute value changes.",
