  "other_facts": "On October 25, 2012, a conditional marketing authorization valid throughout the European Union was issued for brentuximab vedotin for adult patients with relapsed or refractory CD30+ Hodgkin lymphoma and adult patients with relapsed or refractory systemic anaplastic large cell lymphoma. Brentuximab vedotin was evaluated as a single agent. Study SG035-003 included 102 patients with relapsed or refractory Hodgkin lymphoma. Study SG035-004 included 58 patients with relapsed or refractory systemic anaplastic large cell lymphoma. The recommended dose is administered as an intravenous infusion over 30 minutes. Brentuximab vedotin is an antibody-drug conjugate composed of a CD30-directed monoclonal antibody, recombinant chimeric IgG1, covalently linked to the antimicrotubule agent monomethyl auristatin E. Binding of the antibody-drug conjugate to CD30 on the cell surface initiates internalization of the monomethyl auristatin E-CD30 complex, followed by proteolytic cleavage that releases monomethyl auristatin E. In two studies involving 160 patients, partial or complete responses were observed in the majority of patients. At the time of approval, there was no information on the survival of patients treated in the studies, and the responses were considered a clinically relevant benefit. The report summarizes the scientific review of the application leading to approval in the European Union. The detailed scientific assessment report and product information, including the summary of product characteristics, are available on the European Medicines Agency website at http://www.ema.europa.eu.",
