  "other_facts": "Emphysematous renal tract disease (ERTD) is a rare necrotizing infection of the renal parenchyma and urinary tract caused by gas-producing organisms and has life-threatening potential. The objectives were to study the clinical features, radiological classification, and prognostic factors of ERTD and to compare management modalities and outcomes among radiological classes. The patients were seen over the last 3 years in a tertiary care institute in north India. All patients underwent computerized tomography after initial ultrasonography diagnosis and were classified into 5 radiological classes as previously described. Patients who died had severe EPN based on radiological class: 6 had class 3B and 1 had class 4. There was no significant difference between survivor and non-survivor groups with respect to age, gender, duration of diabetes mellitus, duration of symptoms, serum creatinine level, total leukocyte count, hemoglobin, platelet count, and culture positivity.",
