  "other_facts": "A protocol exists for collecting samples to investigate unexplained hypoglycaemia, termed the 'hypopack'. These packs are kept in Accident and Emergency departments and neonatal special care baby units throughout Northern Ireland and most wards of the Regional Children's Hospital. The original retrospective audit included 107 hypopacks received between July 2001 and December 2003 and highlighted problems including samples collected while the patient was receiving dextrose, incomplete clinical history, insufficient samples, haemolysed samples, and poor filing of reports in charts. These problems were addressed by redesigning the request form, updating the protocol, and introducing a summative report. The new protocol was introduced in April 2006. The study aimed to assess whether the revised protocol improved the utility of the hypopack. Provision of information concerning dextrose infusion assisted interpretation of hypopack results.",
