  "safety": null,
  "other_facts": "The prevalence and identification of hypertriglyceridemia in youths will likely increase in the future as a consequence of childhood obesity and increased screening for dyslipidemias. The study sought to review clinical experience with hypertriglyceridemia, evaluate factors associated with increased triglyceride levels, and review treatment options to provide guidance for management. A total of 34 patients received 37 trials of drug therapy as part of triglyceride level management: bile acid-binding resins, n = 12; fibrates, n = 19; statins, n = 6. Lifestyle modifications remain the primary therapeutic avenue for the management of pediatric hypertriglyceridemia, and the authors propose an algorithm for managing this heterogeneous population.",
  "summary": "This clinical review of 76 pediatric patients with elevated triglycerides in a specialized lipid disorders clinic described hypertriglyceridemia etiologies and triglyceride patterns, found that fibrates decreased triglycerides while bile acid-binding resins increased them and statins produced no change, and emphasized lifestyle modification as the primary management approach."
