  "other_facts": "Left ventricular systolic dysfunction is a risk factor for atrial fibrillation, but the atrial cellular electrophysiological mechanisms in humans are unclear. This study investigated whether LVSD in patients in sinus rhythm is associated with atrial cellular electrophysiological changes that could predispose to atrial fibrillation. Right atrial myocytes were obtained from 214 consenting patients in sinus rhythm undergoing cardiac surgery, and action potentials or ion currents were measured using the whole-cell-patch clamp technique. The association between moderate or severe LVSD and shortened atrial cellular effective refractory period was confirmed by multiple linear regression analysis. LVSD in patients in sinus rhythm is independently associated with shortening of atrial cellular effective refractory period, which may be expected to contribute to a predisposition to atrial fibrillation.",
