  "other_facts": "Prevalence rates of cardiometabolic risk factors vary largely among overweight children. Dietary habits were collected. Anthropometry, blood pressure, lipids, fasting and post-load glucose, and insulin were measured. Physical activity was assessed in adolescents using a questionnaire. Plausible reporters consumed more animal protein and sodium and less legumes than recommended in nutritional recommendations, and consumed adequate amounts of fiber mainly derived from whole grains. Subjects skipping breakfast had unhealthy diets and greater body fatness. Hypertensive children consumed less vegetable protein than normotensive children. The cardiometabolic health of obese children improves with vegetable protein and whole grain intake, whereas dysglycemia and adiposity increase with sodium intake.",
