  "other_facts": "IL11 is a crucial factor for human trophoblast function and placentation. Elevated IL11 levels are associated with pregnancy complications including preeclampsia, intrauterine growth restriction (IUGR), and preterm birth. The regulation of IL11 in the placenta had not been investigated. The study examined the effects of pro-inflammatory cytokines IL1β and TNFα and low oxygen tension of 2% on IL11 levels in first trimester placental villous explants. Mass spectrometry was performed on IL11-treated first trimester human placental explants at 100 ng/ml for 24 h with n = 3. PDIA4 is a member of the PDI family and is also known as endoplasmic reticulum stress protein ERP72. GRP78, a master regulator of ER stress, was previously identified in human placenta for the first time. Placental endoplasmic reticulum stress has been postulated in the pathophysiology of preeclampsia and IUGR, but its activation remains elusive. The data suggest that IL11 could trigger an ER stress response in the placenta, which may contribute to obstetric complications such as preeclampsia.",
