  "other_facts": "The questionnaire asked obstetricians how they would manage severe postpartum hemorrhage described in 2 previously validated case-vignettes of different scenarios. Vignette 1 described a typical immediate, severe PPH; vignette 2 described a less typical case of severe but gradual PPH. The vignettes were constructed in 3 successive steps and included multiple-choice questions proposing several types of clinical practice options at each step. Variations in PPH management were assessed in a descriptive analysis. Agreement about management and its timing between vignette 1 and vignette 2 was assessed with the Kappa coefficient; no numerical Kappa value was reported. Analysis showed delayed or inadequate management in both vignettes. Management was inconsistent between the two vignette situations in terms of choice of treatment and timing of almost all treatments. The authors concluded that protocols or procedures are necessary in all maternity units to reduce variations in practices that may explain part of the delay in management leading to PPH-related maternal mortality and morbidity.",
