  "other_facts": "DS-1971a is a highly potent, selective NaV1.7 inhibitor. Exploration of the left-hand phenyl ring of sulfonamide derivatives I and II led to novel cycloalkane derivatives with high NaV1.7 inhibitory potency in vitro. The right-hand heteroaromatic ring affected mechanism-based inhibition liability of CYP3A4; replacement of this moiety generated 4-pyrimidyl derivatives. This modification successfully avoided GSH adduct formation, which can cause idiosyncratic drug toxicity. Additional optimization led to the discovery of DS-1971a. DS-1971a exhibited a favorable toxicological profile, enabling multiple-dose studies in healthy human males, and is expected to exert potent efficacy in patients with peripheral neuropathic pain with a favorable safety profile.",
  "summary": "DS-1971a is a highly potent, selective NaV1.7 inhibitor discovered through medicinal chemistry optimization, with preclinical potency and efficacy and a favorable toxicological profile supporting multiple-dose administration up to 1200 mg/day for 14 days in healthy human males."
}

