  "other_facts": "Previous studies suggested sudomotor dysfunction is closely related to multiple diabetic microvascular complications. The study aimed to investigate the association between sudomotor dysfunction and subclinical carotid atherosclerosis in people with type 2 diabetes. Sudomotor function was assessed using the SUDOSCAN device; sudomotor dysfunction was defined as feet electrochemical skin conductance < 60 μs. The carotid artery was evaluated by high-resolution B-mode ultrasonography; subclinical carotid atherosclerosis was defined as mean carotid intima-media thickness ≥ 1.0 mm and/or presence of carotid plaque. A logistic regression model was used. Among 1788 participants, 429 had sudomotor dysfunction (24.0%). Compared with normal sudomotor function, sudomotor dysfunction had a significantly higher prevalence of subclinical carotid atherosclerosis (68.1% vs 58.3%, p < 0.05). People with subclinical carotid atherosclerosis had a lower median feet electrochemical skin conductance (76.8 μs vs 74.4 μs, p = 0.003) and a higher proportion of abnormal sudomotor function (26.9% vs 19.5%, p < 0.001). The association between sudomotor dysfunction and subclinical carotid atherosclerosis remained significant after adjusting for confounding factors including HbA1c. Sudomotor dysfunction was significantly related to subclinical carotid atherosclerosis in people with type 2 diabetes.",
