  "other_facts": "The purpose was to evaluate the TRI to characterize the risk of death among patients with NSTEMI. The TRI was calculated from baseline age, systolic pressure, and heart rate; it was established in STEMI and is predictive of mortality. Patients presenting with NSTEMI are increasing compared to STEMI and constitute a group with varied risk. Data were from the National Registry of Myocardial Infarction. Values and outcomes were compared between NSTEMI patients and STEMI patients classified by reperfusion status, and baseline characteristics and clinical outcomes were stratified by TRI. The higher mortality risk in NSTEMI compared with STEMI patients treated with reperfusion therapy was explained largely by the higher-risk profile of the NSTEMI population. The TRI provides important information about mortality across the spectrum of myocardial infarction, STEMI and NSTEMI. Early identification of NSTEMI patients at high risk of in-hospital mortality may help initial triage and treatment.",
