  "other_facts": "Research into the interaction between STh and GC-C has generated >100 synthetic analogs of the peptide; several analogs have been investigated as imaging or therapeutic agents for colorectal cancers. In vitro whole-cell crosslinking used 125I-labeled F19-STh(1-19). The putative STh binding protein was significantly smaller than the glycosylated GC-C molecule found in the T84 human colon cancer cell line. Receptor expression in breast cancer cell lines was 40,000-120,000 sites per cell, an abundance equal to or greater than GC-C abundance in colorectal cancer cell lines. STh analog clearance was rapid and primarily via renal excretion into urine. The in vivo model utilized T-47D human breast cancer cell xenografts in SCID mice. The results suggest STh may find application for imaging and treatment of breast cancer.",
