  "other_facts": "Study conducted from March 2003 through December 2005. Objective was to assess whether abciximab is associated with clinical benefit in high-risk patients with ACS undergoing PCI after pretreatment with 600 mg clopidogrel. Context: no specifically designed studies had addressed the role of abciximab in patients with non-ST-segment elevation ACS undergoing PCI after pretreatment with 600 mg clopidogrel. Of 2022 patients enrolled, 1012 were assigned to abciximab and 1010 to placebo. Placebo group received placebo bolus and 12-hour infusion plus heparin bolus 140 U/kg. All patients received clopidogrel 600 mg at least 2 hours before procedure and 500 mg oral or intravenous aspirin. Primary endpoint components were death, myocardial infarction, or urgent target vessel revascularization within 30 days; secondary endpoints were rates of in-hospital major and minor bleeding. Interaction P for troponin subgroup effect was .07. Conclusion: abciximab reduces risk of adverse events in patients with non-ST-segment elevation ACS undergoing PCI after pretreatment with 600 mg clopidogrel, with benefit apparently confined to patients presenting with elevated troponin. Trial registration: ClinicalTrials.gov NCT00133003.",
