  "other_facts": "Risk stratification after myocardial infarction remains expensive and disappointing. Individual patient data were combined from the placebo arms of EMIAT, CAMIAT, TRACE, and DIAMOND-MI. Eligibility included LVEF <=40% or ventricular arrhythmias (>10 ventricular premature beats/hour or a run of ventricular tachycardia). Risk factors for mortality beginning at day 45 post-MI up to 2 years were examined using Cox regression analysis. Risk scores were derived from the equation of a Cox regression model containing only significant variables; the prognostic index was the sum of individual contributions from risk factors. Variables predicting mortality were age, sex, previous MI or angina, hypertension, diabetes, systolic blood pressure, heart rate, NYHA functional class, and non-Q wave infarct on electrocardiogram. Distinct survival curves were obtained for 3 risk groups based on the median and inter-quartile range for the prognostic index. In post-MI patients with LVEF <=40% or frequent ventricular premature beats, the additional use of a simple prognostic indicator based on demographic information provided clinically meaningful risk stratification and may be used to identify patients for prophylactic implantable cardioverter-defibrillator therapy.",
