  "other_facts": "PREDICTIVE stands for Predictable Results and Experience in Diabetes through Intensification and Control to Target: an International Variability Evaluation. The European cohort included 20,531 patients, including 12,981 with type 2 diabetes, prescribed insulin detemir and followed up for 12, 26, or 52 weeks. This analysis reported a subgroup of 2,377 oral antidiabetic drug-treated, insulin-naïve type 2 diabetes patients followed for a mean of 14.4 weeks. Insulin detemir was prescribed by physicians as part of routine clinical care. Improvements in HbA1c, fasting glucose, within-patient fasting glucose variability, and body weight were all statistically significant with p < 0.0001. A significant negative relationship was observed between weight change and baseline BMI, with greater BMI associated with greater weight reduction. Multiple regression analysis showed baseline BMI, baseline HbA1c, and change in HbA1c were predictors of weight change (p < 0.0001 for all), with BMI the strongest predictor. The study concluded that insulin-naïve type 2 diabetes patients can be effectively treated with once-daily insulin detemir (+/- oral antidiabetic drugs) to improve glycaemic control with no adverse effect on weight and a low risk of hypoglycaemia.",
