  "other_facts": "Evaluation of iron status in dialysis patients provides information essential to planning adequate recombinant human erythropoietin treatment; cellular iron status can be determined from the recently available measurement of reticulocyte hemoglobin equivalent (RET-He); RET-He is measured by automated fluorescent flow cytometry in the reticulocyte channel using a polymethine dye; the method also measures the mean value of forward light scatter intensity of mature red blood cells and reticulocytes; these values equate with reticulocyte hemoglobin content; conventional red blood cell parameters and RET-He were measured on a XE-2100 automated blood cell counter (Sysmex); content of reticulocyte hemoglobin (CHr) was measured on an ADVIA120 autoanalyser (Siemens); iron supplements were given to patients with low TSAT or ferritin; the rapid RET-He response within 2 weeks was considered a potential advantage for estimating iron status; RET-He is described as a new parameter equivalent to CHr, easily measurable on a widely spread and popular blood cell counter, and a sensitive and specific marker of iron status in dialysis patients.",
