  "other_facts": "Human leukemic THP-1 promonocytes are widely used as a model for peripheral blood monocytes. Superoxide production during respiratory burst of non-differentiated THP-1 cells is very low. The presented method is rapid and low-cost for measuring chemiluminescence of opsonized zymosan-induced respiratory burst and allows detection of Escherichia coli lipopolysaccharide-induced priming of non-differentiated THP-1 cells based on chemiluminescence reaction kinetics. Four fractions were found to inhibit opsonized zymosan-induced chemiluminescence in a dose-dependent manner, while lactoferrin inhibited chemiluminescence to a lesser extent. Measuring chemiluminescence response of non-differentiated THP-1 cells can serve as a method for screening anti-inflammatory compounds that could be used to reduce the risk of phagocyte-mediated inflammatory diseases.",
  "summary": "An in vitro THP-1 cell study developed a rapid, low-cost chemiluminescence assay for detecting LPS-induced priming and found that protein fractions from Lactobacillus helveticus BGRA43 fermented milk inhibited opsonized zymosan-induced respiratory burst more potently than bovine lactoferrin."
