  "other_facts": "The study evaluated applicability of biomaterials and growth factors to stem cell-based bone regeneration. hBMSCs and hPDLSCs were obtained and identified by stem cell surface markers according to International Society for Cellular Therapy criteria. Each stem cell group was separately treated with serial dilutions of EMD (10, 50, and 100 μg/mL) or rhTGF-β (10 ng/mL). Osteoblastic differentiation was examined by in vitro matrix mineralization using alizarin red staining. mRNA expression of osteopontin and osteonectin was determined by quantitative reverse-transcriptase polymerase chain reaction. hPDLSCs were further assessed for osteocalcin mRNA expression. Stem cells cultured in osteogenic medium were the standard positive control group. In rhTGF-β-supplemented BMSC culture, osteonectin mRNA expression on day 15 was statistically comparable to the positive control group. Extracellular matrix mineralization was inhibited in both groups of stem cells. EMD at 10, 50, or 100 μg/mL had no appreciable effect on osteoblastic differentiation of BMSCs and PDLSCs. Application of rhTGF-β increased osteonectin mRNA expression in BMSCs, supporting the hypothesis that TGF-β might be involved in early osteoblastic maturation.",
