  "other_facts": "Detection of monohydroxy polycyclic aromatic hydrocarbon metabolites in urine is an advisable and valid method to assess human environmental exposure to polycyclic aromatic hydrocarbons. Novel Fe3O4/graphene oxide composites were prepared. Superparamagnetic Fe3O4 nanoparticles provide fast separation to simplify the analytical process. Graphene oxide provides a large functional surface for adsorption. The magnetic nanocomposites were characterized by X-ray diffraction, scanning electron microscopy, transmission electron microscopy, and vibrating sample magnetometry. The experimental conditions were optimized systematically. The method was described as simple, quick, and affordable. It was successfully used in the analysis of human urinary monohydroxy polycyclic aromatic hydrocarbons in two different cities. The results indicated that monohydroxy polycyclic aromatic hydrocarbon levels in human urine can provide useful information for environmental exposure to polycyclic aromatic hydrocarbons.",
