  "other_facts": "Patients with advanced cancer can develop ureteric obstruction. PCN can relieve ureteric obstruction and prevent renal failure, is associated with complications, and can worsen quality of life. Prognostic models of survival after PCN can help identify patients most likely to benefit. Primary objective: assess survival of patients with malignant urinary obstruction after PCN tube insertion. Secondary objectives: identify factors associated with poor prognosis and externally validate an existing model. Univariate factors significantly associated with shorter survival (P < 0.05): type of malignancy, bilateral hydronephrosis, serum albumin <3.5 mg/dL, presence of metastasis, ascites, and pleural effusion. Multivariate Cox proportional hazards regression model factors significantly associated with shorter survival (P < 0.05): type of malignancy, serum albumin <3.5 mg/dL, pleural effusion, and bilateral hydronephrosis. Using serum albumin <3.5 mg/dL, pleural effusion, and bilateral hydronephrosis, patients were stratified into four prognostic groups: zero risk factors 32 patients, one risk factor 85 patients, two risk factors 78 patients, and three risk factors 16 patients; median survival differences across groups were significant (P < 0.0001). The presented prognostic model is an updated model that can be used to identify patients with poor survival after PCN.",
