  "other_facts": "Background: heart rate reduction with ivabradine improves left ventricle filling by prolonging diastolic time and increases stroke volume, while its effect on atrial conduction time and atrial mechanical functions was unclear. Assessments included transthoracic M mode, two-dimensional, pulsed-wave, continuous wave, color flow, and tissue Doppler imaging; left atrial volumes were obtained from apical four-chamber views by the disc method. Left atrial maximum volume was measured at the end-systolic phase, left atrial minimum volume at the end-diastolic phase, and left atrial volume before atrial systole. Calculated parameters: left atrial passive emptying volume = left atrial maximum volume - left atrial volume before atrial systole; left atrial passive emptying fraction = [(left atrial maximum volume - left atrial volume before atrial systole) / left atrial maximum volume] × 100%; left atrial active emptying volume = left atrial volume before atrial systole - left atrial minimum volume; left atrial active emptying fraction = [(left atrial volume before atrial systole - left atrial minimum volume) / left atrial volume before atrial systole] × 100%. The methods report 43 patients as 31 males and 12 females, while the results report 30 men and 13 women.",
