  "other_facts": "Among 705 patients with prostate cancer treated with radical prostatectomy without preoperative hormonal therapy at the authors' institution between 2000 and 2014, 190 (27%) had RM1. Biochemical recurrence was evaluated in 164 patients, excluding 26 patients who underwent adjuvant therapy with or without lymph node metastasis. Evaluated RM1 patients had postoperative prostate-specific antigen <0.2 ng/ml without lymph node metastasis. Survival rates were calculated using the Kaplan-Meier method, multivariate analysis used a Cox regression model, and prediction was assessed using area under the curve of the receiver operating characteristic. Postoperative early ultrasensitive prostate-specific antigen cutoffs were >0.02 ng/ml and <0.01 ng/ml.",
