  "other_facts": "L6 SKMs were divided into control group, H2O2 group, DZ + H2O2 group, and DZ + LY + H2O2 group. H2O2 treatment was 400 μmol/L for 24 h. DZ pre-treatment was 200 μmol/L for 30 min. In the DZ + LY + H2O2 group, DZ and LY294002 were co-administered for 30 min, with LY294002 at 50 μmol/L. Cell apoptosis rates were assessed by flow cytometric analysis. Changes of mitochondrial membrane potential were determined by JC-1 mitochondrial staining. Activation of phosphatidylinositol-3 kinase (PI3K)/Akt, caspase-9, and caspase-3 was detected by western blot. Diazoxide is described as a highly selective mitochondrial ATP-sensitive potassium channel opener known to suppress cell apoptosis and protect cells in oxidative stressed ischemic environments. The DZ-induced cytoprotective and anti-apoptosis effects were partly inhibited by co-administration of the PI3K inhibitor LY294002. The authors concluded that DZ pre-treatment contributes to protection of L6 SKMs against apoptosis at least partly by activating the PI3K/Akt pathway and subsequently inhibiting the mitochondrial-mediated caspase-dependent apoptotic signalling pathway. Transplanted cell survival might greatly improve the therapeutic efficacy of cell therapy.",
