  "other_facts": "Thalassemia and hemoglobinopathies are inherited red blood cell disorders found worldwide. Hemoglobin E disorder has a high prevalence in South East Asia. Most transfusion-dependent thalassemias were genotypically compound heterozygous Hb E/β-thalassemia. In Malaysia, the national screening program for thalassemia was implemented for early pregnancy or secondary school girls; however, many participants do not turn up and missed the screening test. Screening for thalassemia using cord blood samples is an alternative choice because cord blood is a readily available source of blood and enables early detection of disease. Hematological parameters were determined and hemoglobin quantitation for all cord blood samples was performed using capillary electrophoresis system and high performance liquid chromatography. Hemoglobin E was detected in cord blood using capillary electrophoresis system. It can be recommended in areas where Hb E/β is prevalent. Implementation of a screening strategy using capillary electrophoresis on cord blood sampling will identify the disease early. With regular follow-up on these patients, the status of their disease can be determined earlier and appropriate management implemented.",
