  "other_facts": "Accurate measurement of patient weight is important for intravenous alteplase thrombolysis dosing; weight is not measured in most emergency rooms. Alteplase dose was calculated using weight provided by patient or guardian/caregiver, and actual weight was measured after administration. Overused group was defined as stated weight > measured weight; underused group was defined as measured weight >= stated weight. Hemorrhagic transformation on follow-up was determined by gradient-recalled echo MRI or non-enhanced CT. Hemorrhage with progression was defined as an increase in NIHSS by >=4 accompanied by hemorrhage. Predictors were determined using multivariable logistic regression analysis including overused or underused alteplase and baseline clinical and laboratory findings. Model 1 used alteplase overdose as a categorical variable; model 2 used overused alteplase dose as a numerical variable. More alteplase usage than actual weight led to higher hemorrhagic transformation, and alteplase should be administered based on accurately measured weight.",
