  "other_facts": "Septic shock is associated with high mortality of 30%-60%. The study analyzed in-hospital mortality as a function of intensity of vasopressor therapy in a consecutive series of adults with septic shock treated over a four-year period. Receiver operating characteristic curve analysis assessed the overall strength of the intensity-mortality relationship and showed that number of simultaneous vasopressors and vasopressor dose load performed equally well in predicting death or survival. The greater the peak number of vasopressors required, the higher the death rate. When a standard full dose of a vasopressor fails to normalize blood pressure, escalation yields diminishing returns as dose and multiplicity of agents approach practical upper limits. It is not possible to specify a precise cutoff for limiting versus intensifying therapy; mortality of 80% or higher, characterized by two or more concurrent vasopressors at full dose, should prompt shared decision making with the patient's family.",
