  "other_facts": "Background: some effects of dioxins seem different between men and women, and exposures starting at an early age seem to have more prominent effects. Metabolic syndrome was defined as meeting three of the following criteria: fasting glucose ≥100 mg/dl or under treatment for diabetes; waist circumference ≥90 cm in men or ≥80 cm in women; triglycerides ≥150 mg/dl or under treatment for elevated triglycerides; high-density lipoprotein <40 mg/dl in men or <50 mg/dl in women; blood pressures ≥130/85 mmHg or under treatment for hypertension. Positive associations were observed between a high dioxin level and metabolic syndrome. When stratified by gender, a high dioxin level remained an independent predictor of metabolic syndrome in men, but not in women, regardless of the age at starting exposure. Exposure to PCDD/Fs was associated with metabolic syndrome in men, independent of age and age at starting exposure.",
