  "other_facts": "Hypomagnesemia (plasma Mg2+ concentration <0.7 mmol/L) has been described in patients with type 2 diabetes. Polypharmacy is inevitable when treating type 2 diabetes and could explain disturbances in plasma Mg2+ concentration. The study aimed to establish the extent of hypomagnesemia and identify determinants of plasma Mg2+ levels. Plasma Mg2+ concentrations were measured using a spectrophotometric assay. Pearson correlation analyses were used; after excluding confounding variables, all parameters correlating with plasma Mg2+ at P < 0.1 were included in a stepwise backward regression model. Patients using metformin (n = 251, 62%), proton pump inhibitors (n = 179, 45%), or β-adrenergic receptor agonists (n = 31, 8%) displayed reduced plasma Mg2+ levels. Insulin use (n = 299, 76%) positively correlated with plasma Mg2+ levels. Plasma triglycerides and glucose levels were major determinants of plasma Mg2+ concentration. Drug intake explained <10% of hypomagnesemia, excluding polypharmacy as a major cause for hypomagnesemia in type 2 diabetes.",
