  "other_facts": "Sudden increases in serum creatinine after paraquat intoxication have been reported in several clinical studies and may possibly result from creatine-creatinine interconversion related to paraquat toxicity. A liquid chromatography tandem mass spectrometry method with electrospray ionization was developed and validated for simultaneous determination of creatine and creatinine in serum. Chromatographic separation used a Gemini® C6-Phenyl column with gradient elution using 0.1% formic acid in ultrapure water and methanol as the mobile phase. The method had suitable specificity and selectivity. Calibration curves for creatine and creatinine were linear over 0.5-200 µg mL-1. The limit of quantification for both compounds was 0.5 µg mL-1. The method was accurate within a recovery range of 96.23-102.75%, indicating robustness. High creatine concentrations may lead to high serum creatinine despite normal kidney function because creatine is converted to creatinine in proportion to its concentration.",
  "summary": "A validated LC-MS/MS method for serum creatine and creatinine was applied to paraquat-intoxicated patient samples, showing high creatine concentrations that could elevate serum creatinine without kidney dysfunction."
}

