  "other_facts": "Time-to-glucose-peak following the oral glucose tolerance test (OGTT) is described as a highly reproducible marker for diabetes risk. In obese youths, evidence is lacking for the mechanisms underlying the effects of the TCF7L2 rs7903146 variant on glucose peak. Metabolic phenotype and TCF7L2 rs7903146 genotype were analyzed. Participants underwent a 3-hour, 9-point OGTT. The oral minimal model was used to estimate disposition index (DI), static (φstatic) and dynamic (φdynamic) components of beta-cell responsiveness, and insulin sensitivity (SI). In a subgroup of 241 participants longitudinally followed for 2 years, the effect of time-to-glucose-peak on glucose tolerance change was estimated. The authors concluded that the T-risk allele for TCF7L2 rs7903146 prevailed in the late time-to-glucose-peak group, which was associated with impaired beta-cell responsiveness to glucose (φ), thereby predisposing to prediabetes and diabetes in obese youths.",
