  "other_facts": "Background: vitamin D is associated with immune cell growth, vitamin D deficiency has been associated with chronic infections such as tuberculosis, and few studies have examined vitamin D deficiency and opportunistic infection in people living with HIV/AIDS. PWHAs with 25-OH vitamin D test results from 2012 to 2017 were divided into vitamin D-deficient and non-deficient groups by ROC curve analysis; the ROC AUC had P < 0.001; vitamin D deficiency was defined as 25OHD <14 ng/mL; pneumocystis pneumonia was not significantly associated with vitamin D deficiency; the most common opportunistic infection was tuberculosis, followed by pneumocystis pneumonia and cytomegalovirus disease.",
