n ageing (smoking), and considerably increasing burden due to increasing exposure and ageing (ambient particulate matter air pollution, high BMI, high fasting plasma glucose, and high systolic blood pressure); interpretation highlighted progress in maternal and child health, water, sanitation, and handwashing, and household air pollution, need to sustain efforts in low Socio-demographic Index locations, smoking policy success, and urgent need to address ambient particulate matter air pollution, high systolic blood pressure, high fasting plasma glucose, high BMI, obesity, and metabolic syndrome; funding was provided by the Bill & Melinda Gates Foundation.",
