  "other_facts": "Blood products are the current standard for resuscitation of hemorrhagic shock, but perishable blood has logistical constraints that limit availability and prehospital use, making alternatives an active area of investigation. VS-101 is a new PEGylated human hemoglobin-based oxygen carrier designed to avoid the logistical hurdles of traditional blood transfusion. The study sought to determine the safety and ability of VS-101 to maintain circulatory function and capillary oxygen delivery in a severe 50% exchange transfusion model. Comparator lactated Ringer's solution was administered as 50% isovolemic exchange transfusion at 1 mL/kg/min in 8 rats. Interstitial fluid oxygen tension was measured by phosphorescence quenching microscopy in the spinotrapezius muscle. The experimental endpoint was 240 min. The late decrease in tissue oxygenation after 210 min was likely due to VS-101 vascular clearance. VS-101 effectively maintained blood pressure, perfusion, and P ISFo2 with no vasoconstrictive effects in this model. Further elucidation of these beneficial resuscitation effects is warranted to support future clinical trials.",
