  "other_facts": "Over recent decades schizophrenia-spectrum disorder research has focused on early and comprehensive intervention during first episode psychosis, but rural studies are rare. In Greece, mental healthcare in rural areas is mostly delivered by locally-based Mobile Mental Health Units. The study addressed treatment of first episode psychosis patients by MMHUs in rural Greece, focusing on first episode schizophrenia. Nine MMHUs participated across rural mainland and some islands of Greece. The percentage of patients seeking help from MMHUs was low compared with expected cases, and the attendance rate was high among those examined, without reported numerical values. Further research on psychosis/schizophrenia in rural contexts is warranted.",
  "summary": "In a multicenter retrospective observational study of 216 patients with non-affective psychosis treated by nine Greek mobile mental health units, 153 had schizophrenia and follow-up showed high engagement, age-related differences in treatment continuation, and a 47.22% reduction in hospital admissions."
}

