  "other_facts": "Pediatric hypertension predicts adult hypertension and early target organ damage; global prevalence estimates based on different diagnostic principles remain scarce. Several databases, including PubMed, Web of Science, Embase, the China National Knowledge Infrastructure (CNKI), and the Wanfang Database, were systematically searched from inception to July 7, 2024. Studies were included if they were original investigations in children and adolescents younger than 19 years, represented the general population, and provided data on hypertension prevalence. Data screening and extraction were performed independently by 2 authors. A random-effects model was used to estimate prevalence. Temporal trends, regional differences, and population differences were explored. Subgroup analyses and meta-regression analyses were performed to identify sources of heterogeneity. Publication bias was assessed by funnel plots and the Egger test. Significant differences were observed across geographical regions and population characteristics for the prevalence of pediatric hypertension. The study highlights the importance of measurements on multiple occasions to enhance reliability and the necessity for targeted interventions to promote healthy lifestyles because of prevalence differences across body mass index values.",
